  "body": "### What changed\n\n- `stock_sim::cut::simulate` no longer copies the column stock's whole cut history at the start of each call. It takes the history out, grows it with `Arc::make_mut`, and puts it back. `Arc::make_mut` copies the history only when another stock shares it.\n- On a refusal, the code truncates the cuts to their old count and puts the history back. `add_ops` only appends cuts, so the stock stays as it was.\n- The behaviour of a single call does not change. A program that is cut one move for each call is now linear in its moves, not quadratic.\n\n### Readings\n\n- New pin `a_call_grows_the_history_in_place` on the v0.26.0 code: FAILED (`simulate copied the history instead of growing it in place`). With this change: ok.\n- 4000 one-move calls on a 200 x 200 column block (debug build, this machine): 1.649 s before, 0.514 s after. The stock is the same to the bit as the one-call cut, before and after.\n- A 3-axis job of 137,940 moves on a 2541 x 2100 column stock, cut one move for each call: more than 1800 s before (stopped), 6 s after. The removed volume is the same to the bit as the one-call cut.\n\n### Pinning tests\n\n- `stock_sim::cut::history_tests::a_call_grows_the_history_in_place`: the history keeps its allocation across two calls, and the cuts are added.\n- `stock_sim::cut::history_tests::a_shared_history_is_copied_before_it_grows`: a clone keeps its own history and its columns when the other stock is cut.\n- `stock_columns::one_move_for_each_call_is_the_one_call_cut`: 4000 one-move calls give the one-call stock to the bit. This test joins the existing `stock_columns` binary. It adds no new test binary.\n\n### Gates\n\n- Quick gate on the final head (ffe6b6e86, after a merge of upstream main): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 83 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (20.8 min).\n- Pinning tests on the final head: `history_tests` 2/2, `stock_columns` 4/4.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the final head: clean.\n- Light gate (`cargo xtask gate light`) on the first head e8f8d3b2c: 4 steps, 0 failed. The merge of main added no code of this PR.\n- The new pin on the v0.26.0 `cut.rs`: FAILED, as expected. On this branch: ok.\n\n### Not exercised\n\n- The field engine and the carried stock. `carried::clip_columns_under` has the same copy, but it runs one time for each setup, not for each move. This PR does not change it.\n- The heavy lanes (they run at the cut).\n- The refusal path is not reached by a test: `check_ops` and the posed-move check refuse before the history changes, and I found no input that makes `add_ops` or `read` refuse after the history is taken out.\n\nFork synced at v0.26.0. The branch was refreshed with a merge of upstream main (contributor mode: merge, no rebase). The two conflicts were in process files only (`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`); main's version was taken. The diff against main is now the three files of this fix.\n\nChangelog: Cutting a program one move at a time on a column stock is no longer quadratic in the moves.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3819\n",
